<title>UK: Ontario sets 3.0 bln French franc 12-year bond.</title>
<headline>Ontario sets 3.0 bln French franc 12-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers Morgan Stanley and Societe Generale.</p>
<p> BORROWER   PROVINCE OF ONTARIO</p>
<p> AMT    3.0 BLN FFR   COUPON     5.875     MATURITY    21.JUL.09</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  100.794   PAY DATE    21.JUL.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  2.0	 REOFFER    99.144    SPREAD	+22</p>
<p> MOODY	AA3	 LISTING    PARIS     PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AA-	 DENOMS (K) 10-100-1M SALE LIMITS *</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ONTARIO   HOME CTRY  CANADA    TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.35	SELL CONC  1.65	PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND INTERPOLATED 8.5 OCT.08 AND 6.5 APR.11  NOTES     *AS PER ONTARIO'S EMTN DOCUMENTATION.</p>
<p>		THERE IS A REDENOMINATION CLAUSE</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
